Does anyone have some advice for further debugging?

soundcard: cardbus card, via pci adapter card
driver: snd_hdsp, yenta_cardbus
cpu: AMD  A10-5700

Further information can be found in appended output of lspci -vv and
/proc/cpuinfo.

The device is detected and can be configured, but after that commit it
just produces
silence (playback / recording, both using dma). No change in dmesg output, apart
from the additional 3-line block about PCI-DMA using SWIOTLB (the appended
dmesg output is for 3.8.4-rt1, the rt patch makes no difference).

As a shot into the dark I tried following hack, which seems to work (for me...):

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--- a/drivers/iommu/amd_iommu.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/amd_iommu.c
@@ -3169,6 +3169,7 @@ int __init amd_iommu_init_dma_ops(void)
        swiotlb = 0;

        /* Make the driver finally visible to the drivers */
+       dma_ops = &amd_iommu_dma_ops;
        unhandled = device_dma_ops_init();
        if (unhandled && max_pfn > MAX_DMA32_PFN) {
                /* There are unhandled devices - initialize swiotlb for them */
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The soundcard device is not in the initial list of pci devices handled
by amd_iommu_init_dma_ops(). Later on device_change_notifier() is
called for that device with BUS_NOTIFY_ADD_DEVICE, but the
protection domain is already set, so dev->archdata.dma_ops is
not set in that call (result of some printk-debugging).

I'm lost here since I not familiar with the kernel code.. any advice
appreciated.

regards
Andreas

